  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Core polymer 3D printing demand is facing headwinds from unfavorable foreign exchange and tariffs, which dampened the top line and compressed profitability. Despite this, Stratasys is expanding its industrial materials portfolio with a new flame-retardant composite for rail and transportation, targeting a specialized, high-value vertical that could open fresh revenue channels and improve system utilization on its high-end printers. This push into regulated end-use applications provides some offset to broader macro caution weighing on near‑term spending.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership reiterated its full‑year 2026 outlook in the face of a soft first quarter, signaling confidence in an eventual recovery or effective cost control. The company maintains a debt‑free balance sheet with ample cash, preserving strategic flexibility to invest in R&D and application‑specific material launches. Analyst sentiment is moderately constructive—consensus rates the stock a “Moderate Buy”—though recent price‑target reductions reflect some skepticism; the consistent guidance posture helps steady credibility as execution unfolds against macro friction.",
